From 366058f9d3ad5ca32056cac1fcad49abfb80e3af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 15:32:25 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] yblod-engine-vk: no nearest EL upscale (bilinear
 instead)

The FEL EL upscale is now Annex B (Master Reference, el_scaler 1) or
bilinear (el_scaler 2). el_scaler 0, which was nearest, plans as bilinear,
so callers that still ask for it (Kodi's dvbridge.elnearest, DV_EL_SCALER=
nearest) get the cheaper upscale instead of failing. Every nearest branch
is gone from the shaders (EL filter codes: 0 Annex B, 2 bilinear).

Tests: nearest_requests_plan_bilinear (el_scaler 0 and 2 give identical
plans, every fixture and configuration); the planner's golden digests for
the configurations that requested nearest (0, 4, 5) regenerated, config 0
now el_scaler 2 and equal to the previous bilinear plan's digest; Annex B
and bilinear GPU output byte-identical to before. yblod's OpenCL engine and
CPU reference keep their own nearest.
